This research proposes an efficient cylinder harvester made of Lshaped piezoelectric coupled beams by fully using the positive piezoelectric effect of the piezoelectric patch. Based on the proposed harvester, a series of experiment specimens are designed and manufactured, the effects of some parameters on the output electric parameters from the harvester are studied through comprehensive experiments. According to the experimental results, some valuable conclusions can be drawn as following:

1. The output voltages from an L-shaped beam of the harvester increase with the decrease of the substrate thickness and the increase of the PZT4 patch thickness, the output voltage densities from an L-shaped beam increase with the decrease of the thicknesses of the PZT4 patch and its substrate and the PCS length;   
2. The output power and power density from an L-shaped beam of the harvester sharply increase with the decrease of the thicknesses of the PZT4 patch and its substrate, but the output power slightly increases with the increase of the PCS length;   
3. The increase of the PCS length hardly has influence on the output voltage and the output power density from an L-shaped beam of the harvester;   
4. The peak-to-peak voltage (voltage density) and the output power (power density) from an L-shaped beam of the harvester can reach up to $5 0 \mathrm { ~ V ~ } ( 0 . 2 0 2 \mathrm { ~ V } / \mathrm { m m } ^ { 3 } )$ and $2 . 3 5 ~ \mathrm { m W }$ $( 9 . 5 1 ~ \mu \mathsf { W } /$ $\mathrm { m m } ^ { 3 }$ for a PZT4 patch with a dimension of $3 8 \mathrm { m m } \times 1 3 \mathrm { m m } \times 0 . 5 \mathrm { m m }$ .
